A Mac behind the firewall rowt exists for, for `doctor`: over the NIC Google
times out (curl 28), GitHub fails the handshake (curl 35), Baidu answers, and the
API answers 403 — refused by region, which `_dr_served` counts as NOT served;
over the default route (the old VPN) the API answers 200. So: GITHUB_BLOCKED,
AGENT_API_NEEDS_TUNNEL, and then one of two: AGENT_VIA_VPN when the shell has no
proxy variable, AGENT_VIA_PROXY_ENV when the case sets HTTPS_PROXY (rowt's own
port follows rowt; another port stops with its app, and its `user:pass@` is
masked). The cli-diff token for that variable exists for this scenario.
